{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip deviated, and the deviation is established under POL-RD-01 on the trace figure, which governs. The trace records 9.56 km between the recorded pickup event and the recorded dropoff event; the platform optimal stored on the trip record at booking is 7.4 km. Excess = 2.16 km and 29.19% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates are cleared: the excess is greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km absolute, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trip record's actual_distance_km of 9.6 is the rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and is deliberately not relied on for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess stands on the trace alone. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 130 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gap between consecutive fixes above 10 seconds, the largest straight-line step between consecutive fixes 122.3 m, and the highest implied speed 44.0 km/h. None of limbs (a), (b) or (c) of POL-RD-07 is met, so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No external-traffic exoneration is available to reduce this excess. The only traffic-advisory artifact in the bundle is EV-ADVIS-04001-01, which is MISSING: it has no payload and carries weight 0.0. There is accordingly no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, with a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle reaching that segment, matched by a route leaving and re-joining the optimal corridor, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. The driver's statement does not assert a traffic cause at all; had one been asserted, POL-RD-13 would discard it for want of the advisory record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-04001-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log is IMPAIRED: weight_multiplier 0.85, issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY (MSG-04001-002 mixes Malay 'singgah' and 'kejap' with English), and I disclose that discount. What it shows is a request for a stop, not a request for a route: 'later can singgah Jurong Point kejap? need to collect parcel at the POPStation, 3 min only', answered by the driver 'ok can, I drop you at the taxi stand side'. Under POL-RD-04 only the excess distance between leaving and re-joining the optimal corridor is excluded; the rider never authorised 2.16 km of additional driving, and the driver's account of what happened cites no evidence ID in his statement, so under POL-RD-08 that assertion carries no weight and is discarded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-04001", "EV-GPS-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantum of any POL-RD-04 exclusion is not on this record and must not be invented. The waypoint_approach block reports only the nearest fix to the requested waypoint — 49.8 m, at 10:18:02 — and nothing in the bundle identifies where the vehicle left the optimal corridor or where it re-joined it. With no measured leave-and-rejoin stretch, the excess cannot be adjusted down on the evidence as it stands, and the figure that governs POL-RD-02 remains the measured 2.16 km against the booked optimal of 7.4 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. The fare model on the fare breakdown is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs (not POL-RD-11), and the surge multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which is 1.0. Recomputed fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 7.4 + 0.28 x 15) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 fixed surcharge - 0 promo discount = 13.55 + 0.80 = 14.35. Charged total is 17.65, so the refund is 17.65 - 14.35 = 3.30. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis (so the outcome is not NO_ACTION) and is 18.7% of charged_total, far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome for the filing rider is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.30, rounded up to the nearest 0.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is added on top of that figure and nothing is double-counted. The fare breakdown's ERP block shows on-optimal-route total 0.00 and off-optimal-route total 0.00 with no gantry lines, there is no airport surcharge (the trip neither originates nor terminates at an airport), and the waiting-time fee is 0.00, so the POL-RD-09 pass-through correction is nil and the distance-and-time refund of 3.30 stands alone as the entire monetary correction.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-10 trigger fires and the case can be ruled on. The trip identifier matches across the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown; the timestamps are consistent and causally ordered, with the trace's first fix equal to started_at 10:12:40 and its last fix equal to ended_at 10:33:55; the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c); every charge line has a counterpart on the record; and the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-04001", "EV-GPS-04001", "EV-FARE-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Confidence is not capped below the platform floor. The artifacts that carry the deciding facts — the trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is 1.0 and the 0.70 escalation floor is not reached; the only impaired artifact on the bundle is the chat log at 0.85 with issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, and it does not carry the deciding fact of the measured excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001", "EV-FARE-04001", "EV-CHAT-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The detour the rider now disputes is one the rider herself ordered. MSG-04001-002 in EV-CHAT-04001 was sent by the RIDER at 10:11:40 and reads 'uncle later can singgah Jurong Point kejap? need to collect parcel at the POPStation, 3 min only'; it carries waypoint_hint Jurong Point (1.33975, 103.7064), which the platform itself resolved from the message text at ingest. That satisfies POL-RD-04(a), the instruction comes from the rider, and POL-RD-04(c), it identifies a place specifically enough to act on. It is not one of the vague messages the clause excludes. EV-CHAT-04001 is impaired and I disclose it rather than present it as clean: admissibility status IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.85, issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, because MSG-04001-002 mixes Malay ('singgah', 'kejap') with English. Even at that discount the artifact sits well above the platform's 0.70 confidence floor, and the driver's acceptance, MSG-04001-003, is in plain English.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The instruction came before the vehicle left the optimal corridor, which is what POL-RD-04(b) requires. MSG-04001-002 was sent at 10:11:40; the trip did not start until 10:12:40, when the rider came on board (EV-TRIP-04001, trip_started event); and even the driver's assent, MSG-04001-003, was sent at 10:12:00, still before departure. The vehicle therefore left the corridor on the rider's instruction and not on the driver's own initiative. (EV-CHAT-04001 carries the impairment disclosed above: IMPAIRED, weight 0.85, LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04's corroboration test is satisfied on the platform's own computation. Fix 33 of EV-GPS-04001, at 10:18:02, lies 49.83 m from the requested waypoint - well inside the clause's 200 m threshold - so the vehicle did pass within 200 m of the place the rider named, exactly as POL-RD-04 demands. The geometry comes from EV-GPS-04001, a COMPLETE artifact at weight 1.0 (130 fixes, 10 s cadence, no gaps); the instruction it corroborates comes from EV-CHAT-04001, impaired at 0.85 for LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, which I disclose.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-CHAT-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The stop actually happened, and the rider's own messages say so. She asked for three minutes (MSG-04001-002), and at 10:20:45 she sent MSG-04001-004: 'ok got it, coming back to the car now'. That sentence only makes sense if she had left the vehicle at the requested stop and was returning to it. The driver's account - he waited at the taxi stand about three minutes and then drove on to Bukit Batok - matches both the chat and the trace. (EV-CHAT-04001 is impaired: IMPAIRED, weight 0.85, LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the detour was rider-requested and corroborated, POL-RD-04 excludes the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor 'before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied', and on this record that is the whole of the measured excess. The platform's own derived deviation is 2.16 km, or 29.19%, against the 7.4 km booked optimal - above the 0.8 km and 20% establishment gates of POL-RD-01 but far below its 8.0 km and 50% materiality gates, so POL-RD-06 never engages. The rider's own narrative describes a single loop ('one big round'), the only stop the record contains is the Jurong Point waypoint the trace approaches, and nothing in the evidence identifies any second departure from the corridor. Exclude that excess and no deviation survives POL-RD-01, no refund arithmetic under POL-RD-02 is reached, and the rider's claim fails.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-CHAT-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 shifts the burden to the driver once the rider shows a threshold excess, and the driver discharges it in exactly the way that clause requires: by pointing to a specific artifact and a specific clause. The artifact is EV-CHAT-04001, message MSG-04001-002, the rider's request with its platform-resolved waypoint_hint, corroborated by the waypoint-approach computation in EV-GPS-04001; the clause is POL-RD-04. This is not the bare 'traffic was bad' assertion POL-RD-08 refuses to entertain. It is rider causation, evidenced by the rider's own message and by the trace's approach to the point she named.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-04001", "EV-GPS-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern may be found against this driver on the fields POL-RD-06 names. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, against a trigger of 3 flags, and 0 flags over 260 completed_trips_90d is a ratio of 0 against a trigger of 0.05, with completed_trips_90d of 260 well above the clause's 40-trip minimum. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (1) is a different field and is not the trailing-90-day figure the clause asks for; POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting it. POL-RD-06 is in any event not engaged on materiality, because the excess of 2.16 km is under both the 8.0 km and the 50% materiality gates of POL-RD-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing defect to correct and no bad faith to hold against the driver. EV-FARE-04001 reconciles to the cent: 3.80 base fare + 7.17 distance on 9.56 km + 5.88 time on 21 min + 0.80 platform fee = 17.65. distance_charged_km 9.56 equals the trace distance of 9.56, so no distance went unbilled and none was inflated; there are no ERP or toll lines and no gantry the trace never crossed; and waiting_time_fee is 0.00, so the driver did not bill the rider a cent for the three minutes she asked him to wait. Nothing on the fare artifact supports a pass-through or billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04001", "EV-GPS-04001", "EV-TRIP-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No mandatory escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 is engaged. The gps_trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 130 fixes at a 10 s cadence, a largest interval of 10 s against a 90 s limit, and a largest straight-line step of 122.3 m against a 500 m limit, so POL-RD-10(3) has no purchase and the measured excess and the corroboration both rest on an ungapped trace. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-04001-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 because no advisory was retrieved for this trip, and that absence costs the driver nothing: he asserts no external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 is neither invoked nor needed, and POL-RD-13 confirms that an advisory cited by no party as an exculpatory record is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradiction POL-RD-10(5) describes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-04001", "EV-ADVIS-04001-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The present state is a charge that stands: EV-FARE-04001 records payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. On a rider-filed dispute over this fare, NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03 leaves that state exactly as it is, so the metered fare remains with the driver who earned it. Since the deviation is exonerated under POL-RD-04, no billing-integrity defect exists under POL-RD-09, and no escalation trigger fires, that is the outcome this record supports.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-04001"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

