    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both of you. It concerns trip TRP-04001, Pioneer MRT Station to Bukit Batok West Ave 6 on 22 Aug 2026.\n\nOn the measured evidence a route deviation is established. The GPS trace EV-GPS-04001 records 9.56 km against the booked platform optimal of 7.4 km stored on EV-TRIP-04001, an excess of 2.16 km, or 29.2% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km) and is below the materiality gates, so it is an established but not a material deviation. Taken alone, POL-RD-02 would recompute the metered fare as 3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.4 (5.55) + 0.28 x 15 (4.20) + 0.80 platform fee = 14.35, against the charged total of 17.65 on EV-FARE-04001, giving a refund of 3.30 — the figure the rider's advocate asked me to award.\n\nI do not award it, because POL-RD-04 exonerates the excess. The rider herself asked for the detour. Her message MSG-04001-002 in EV-CHAT-04001, sent at 10:11:40 before the vehicle moved (the trip started at 10:12:40), asks the driver to stop at Jurong Point to collect a parcel and carries the platform-resolved waypoint_hint that POL-RD-04 requires; the driver agreed at 10:12:00; and the trace corroborates it, fix 33 at 10:18:02 lying 49.8 m from the waypoint, inside the clause's 200 m threshold. Limb (a) the instruction came from the rider, limb (b) it was given before the vehicle left the optimal corridor, and limb (c) it names a place specifically enough to act on, are all met, and the message is not one of the vague instructions the clause excludes. The excess the rider now disputes is the trip to the point she herself named, so it is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied, and no deviation survives the exclusion.\n\nThe rider's argument that the size of the exclusion is not on the record, so the measured 2.16 km must stand, is not accepted. The record identifies one departure from the optimal corridor — to the waypoint the rider named — and no second detour is evidenced by any artifact; the rider's assertion of a larger 'one big round' is not carried by the trace, the trip record or the chat, and the driver denied it. There is therefore nothing to separate out, and the whole of the measured excess is attributable to the rider's own instruction.\n\nDisclosure and confidence. The chat log EV-CHAT-04001 is impaired and I name it: weight_multiplier 0.85, issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, because MSG-04001-002 mixes Malay ('singgah', 'kejap') with English. That artifact carries the deciding fact — the rider's detour request — and my confidence is capped at 0.85 by it. The finding survives the discount: the request and the driver's plain-English reply MSG-04001-003 are clear enough, and the trace (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) independently puts the vehicle at the requested point. 0.85 is above the 0.70 escalation floor, so the case does not escalate.\n\nOn the remaining claims: the fare reconciles to the cent with no ERP, no toll, no airport surcharge and no waiting-time charge (waiting_time_fee 0.00), so there is no POL-RD-09 pass-through or billing-integrity correction and no referral on that ground. No repeat-deviation pattern can be found under POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against a trigger of 3, and 0 over 260 completed trips in 90 days is a ratio of 0 against a trigger of 0.05; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the field that clause names and I have not substituted it. Nothing was billed for distance the trace does not record, so no driver compensation is payable under POL-RD-04. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the identifiers match, the timestamps are causally ordered, the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07, the refund would be far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling, and no traffic advisory was on file or relied on. The trace being policy-clean is stated separately from the chat log being down-weighted.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The metered charge of SGD 17.65 on EV-FARE-04001 stands, no refund issues to the rider, no compensation is payable to the driver, and the rider's claim is not supported. Either party may appeal this provisional ruling once under POL-GEN-04."
  },
