{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.3,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "The route. The GPS trace for this trip records 9.56 km driven between the recorded pickup and drop-off, against the 7.4 km optimal route stored on the trip record at booking; the trace figure governs and the trip record's 9.6 km is only a rounded copy of it. The excess is 2.16 km, or 29.2% of the optimal route — more than 20% and more than 0.8 km, so both limbs of POL-RD-01 are cleared and a deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (under 50% and under 8.0 km), so the driver-profile check under POL-RD-06 is not engaged, and in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 260 completed trips, so no repeat pattern is established and no conduct referral arises.\n\nThe Jurong Point stop. The driver is right that the stop was requested, and the rider is wrong to treat it as a driver's invention: MSG-04001-002 in EV-CHAT-04001 was sent by the rider at 10:11:40, before the trip started at 10:12:40, asks the driver to stop at Jurong Point, and carries the platform-resolved waypoint_hint for Jurong Point; the trace passes 49.8 m from that waypoint at 10:18:02, well inside the 200 m test POL-RD-04 sets, and the rider's own later message shows the stop happened. POL-RD-04 is therefore available and its (a), (b) and (c) conditions are met — the driver is not penalised for making the stop he was asked to make. But POL-RD-04 excludes only 'the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor', and nothing in this bundle measures where the vehicle left the optimal corridor or where it rejoined it: the platform's own derived waypoint block reports only the nearest fix to the waypoint, and I must not invent a leave-and-rejoin stretch or an adjusted optimal that is not on the record. The measured excess therefore stands, and the driver's bare assertion in his statement that he 'never go round anywhere' does not explain the 2.16 km. In short, the rider asked for a brief stop, not for 2.16 km of extra driving, so no part of the excess is excluded on the evidence as it stands.\n\nAmounts, on separate lines as POL-RD-02 requires. Charged_total: 17.65. Recomputed_fare: (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 7.4 km + 0.28 x 15 min) x surge 1.0 (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 13.55 + 0.80 = 14.35. Refund: 17.65 - 14.35 = 3.30. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 (not POL-RD-11) governs; 3.30 is above the 0.50 de minimis and is 18.7% of the charge, below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome for the rider is PARTIAL_REFUND of 3.30, rounded up to the nearest 0.05. Nothing is added on top: there are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines and no gantry charged that the trace never crossed, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and produces no billing-integrity referral. No driver compensation arises either — the distance billed (9.56 km) equals the distance driven, so there is no unbilled shortfall.\n\nImpairment, named as POL-GEN-02 requires. The chat log EV-CHAT-04001 carries weight 0.85 for issue LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY (MSG-04001-002 mixes Malay and English). It is the lowest-weighted artifact this ruling relies on — the ruling has to decide what the rider actually instructed and whether it explains the excess — so confidence is capped at 0.85 and held there; the rider's submission that confidence may stand at 1.0 is not accepted. 0.85 is above the 0.70 floor, so the case is decided and not escalated, and the finding survives the discount. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-04001-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0: no party relies on it for exculpation (the driver asserts no traffic cause at all), so it decides nothing, and POL-RD-13 confirms that its absence is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradiction POL-RD-10(5) describes. The GPS trace is COMPLETE and is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 130 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gap over 10 s, largest step 122.3 m — so the excess needs no independent corroboration and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers match across the three instruments, timestamps are consistent and causally ordered, and the refund is far below both 150.00 and the charged total.\n\nBecause 3.30 is below the 8.00 execution threshold, it is released automatically on issue. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
